  "body": "What happens: on upstream main e74bca1f (Merge PR #1306), `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test stepped_stock_rapid` fails 1 of 8 tests:\n\n```\na_coarse_stock_whose_source_is_gone_is_never_acquitted\npanicked at crates/app/tests/stepped_stock_rapid.rs:274:23:\nPart: not blocked by the rapid law: post blocked - Op1: model 'casting' was imported too coarsely to verify; re-import with a larger STEP facet budget (surfaces are approximated to within 2.500 mm)\n```\n\nThe post is still blocked, so nothing unsafe gets through. But the test expects the rapid-in-stock law to name the blocking (`rapid move <at> `), and a coarse-import refusal now fires first. Either the test should accept that refusal, or the order of the refusals changed by accident. A merge since the test was written (#1098 review, commits 45acac0d and 3c65821a) has changed which refusal wins.\n\nEvidence: found while gating PR #1139 (quick tier). It reproduces on plain upstream/main with that PR's changes absent.\n\nDone means: the test is green on main, and both the rapid law and the coarse-import refusal are pinned to block this program by name, with the intended order recorded.\n",
